emit_nt_cfind1n:
    # rdi=s rsi=st rdx=lim rcx=ch -> rax = first index in [st, lim) whose
    # byte equals ch, else -1 (0 when s is 0). SWAR 8-byte scan: xor the
    # qword with ch broadcast, classic haszero mask ((x-0x0101..)&~x&
    # 0x8080..); the LOWEST set byte of that mask is always a real match
    # (borrows only flag bytes after a true zero), so bsf+shr3 gives the
    # first hit directly. 8-byte loads stay inside [st,lim), so there is
    # no NUL overread and no alignment requirement. Volatile-only leaf
    # (rax rcx rdx r8-r11); assembled+diff-verified in scripts/swar_twins.s
    # (550k randomized differential cases vs the byte-loop reference).
    emit:
        72 137 248 72 133 255 15 132 136 0 0 0 15 182 201 73
        184 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 76 15 175 193 73 185 1
        1 1 1 1 1 1 1 73 186 128 128 128 128 128 128 128
        128 76 141 28 55 72 141 20 23 73 141 67 8 72 57 208
        119 46 73 139 3 76 49 192 72 137 193 76 41 201 72 247
        208 72 33 193 76 33 209 116 17 72 15 188 201 72 193 233
        3 73 141 4 11 72 41 248 235 42 73 131 195 8 235 201
        73 57 211 115 22 65 15 182 3 68 56 192 116 5 73 255
        195 235 237 76 137 216 72 41 248 235 9 72 199 192 255 255
        255 255 235 0
    leave()
    ret()
    return 1

